# Line-ending and binary handling.
#
# This file exists because of a real defect: with `core.autocrlf=true` and no
# .gitattributes, git treated the app's icons as text and stripped every \r
# byte from them. 35 of 37 tracked PNGs were corrupted *in the committed
# blobs* — their signature read `89 50 4E 47 0A 1A 0A` instead of
# `89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A`.
#
# Debug builds hid it (they skip PNG crunching), so it only surfaced as
# "AAPT: error: file failed to compile" on the first release build.

# Normalize text in the repository, and let git decide per-file.
* text=auto

# Explicitly binary — never transform these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.so binary
*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.parquet binary
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.safetensors binary
*.pt binary
*.bin binary

# Scripts that must keep LF regardless of platform, or they fail to execute.
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Notebooks are JSON; diffing them is noisy but they are text.
*.ipynb text

# Generated lockfiles — keep them stable across platforms.
pubspec.lock text eol=lf
